{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-excellent-nagata}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6c17237c6dcb26efd35ea1cfef98de198ac491d9ac89925c127b9568f2880074", "source_text": "A quasi-excellent scheme is Nagata.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e672a50dcc0e23613393f803981ca7faf31f6f42a69ce5b684d3463c9bf0b27c", "unit_id": "tag:0HA9:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-quasi-excellent-nagata}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:039e03d949b744b92b572e6b775db4034220d6d5e7bc253ebc7207e28815371d", "source_text": "See More on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c8b357af5630b1a5d08780c2b7b8a8f960b1a0f8278839de7ac7f47c2d9d4e1b", "unit_id": "tag:0HA9:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-excellent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b3055ea2944ed5fcda6131396aa9e9e6d3ca5169ca39bc6c9f17b2efc3c1e8ce", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bbd0c42666b3a58912eecaa5836abf8241e216f0358de6d23be69bd450148d88", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is excellent, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is quasi-excellent and universally catenary.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:41ea7ae22c2e7f11988b87c9654548483c5b4c3ef959152ab1777084110ea8f5", "unit_id": "tag:0HAA:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in U \\subset X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-universally-catenary-local}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-universally-catenary-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2488a4b2fedf1302fefed64db8e00f772d8dcc236729c335dfd92fe7cab911e1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c0e0616d7696b565ca9b5c127aa13ea7c629f45240311540233687097383c454", "source_text": "Assume (1). Since excellent rings are quasi-excellent, it is clear\nthat <MATH_0001> is quasi-excellent. Since excellent rings are universally\ncatenary, it also follows that <MATH_0002> is universally catenary by\nLemma <REF_0001>. Assume (2).\nLet <MATH_0003>. Since <MATH_0004> is quasi-excellent there exists\nan affine open neighbourhood <MATH_0005>\nsuch that <MATH_0006> is quasi-excellent. Since\n<MATH_0007> is universally category, the ring <MATH_0008> is also\nuniversally catenary by Lemma <REF_0002>,\nwhence excellent.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6eb02fbce69f80e2158fed01f7e41f14a9b0000efc2c4d8ee3b60b420f987b30", "unit_id": "tag:0HAA:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-excellent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b3c30cfe5c4a198978617865378dfb5fb8a2781d244cee7f5cd6823e9358f521", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is (quasi-)excellent.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nis (quasi-)excellent.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005> such that\neach <MATH_0006> is (quasi-)excellent.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is (quasi-)excellent.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is (quasi-)excellent then every open subscheme\nis (quasi-)excellent.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:84344d83ebd5070455b8dd1dd0aea507ce4b2ab9880edb956a73b4d487c7b430", "unit_id": "tag:0HAB:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-quasi-excellent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-J}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{properties-lemma-locally-G-scheme}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-excellent}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-universally-catenary-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a4af8bf203d64d10b1ea3b51f3c93d2d2b55d7574ec5e1ad71e24f71c0558d4d", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001> being\nquasi-excellent is the same as being a G-scheme and J-2.\nThus for the quasi-excellent case, the lemma follows from\nLemma <REF_0002> and\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nFor the excellent case, use Lemma <REF_0004>,\nthe quasi-excellent case, and Lemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c547a0ca720b7d0157508a48f4c04df26873fae8980401ffe78d98192f2d0d0a", "unit_id": "tag:0HAB:proof"}
